    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1300">

                <pb facs="0886" n="770" xml:id="pg770"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/10618.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé O’Shaughnessy to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul at Progreso telegraphs as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>January 14. Mexican de facto authorities in the name of President called
                            all the merchants and private landowners to the Government offices and
                            required immediately sixty day loans for the purpose carrying on the
                            northern campaign. Foreigners being obliged to contribute same as
                            Mexicans practically enforced because of fear damage business if
                            refused. Progreso contributions approximately thirty thousand pesos.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
